## Audi’s History of Mechanical Problems

Audi, a subsidiary of the Volkswagen Group, has produced some of the most high-end vehicles in the world. Audi has always led the way in terms of tech advancements and performance.

Despite its reputation, some Audi models have been plagued by recurring issues over the years. These issues have ranged from engine malfunctions and electrical problems to airbags and fuel system defects.

Some of the most recalled models - and the ones with the most Audi lemon law complaints - include:

## Audi A6 - The Most Recalled Audi Model

The Audi A6 has been in production since 1994 and has amassed a [total of 36 recalls](https://www.cars.com/research/audi-a6/recalls/) (as of this writing). Issues with the A6 have stretched across multiple generations. While this model is known for its elegance and performance, it has been prone to several common defects, including:

- Electrical System Problems

- Airbag Defects

- Engine Cooling Issues

- Fuel System Malfunctions

- Excessive Oil Consumption

If you’re one of the many Audi owners experiencing recurring problems with any of these systems, your Audi A6 may qualify as a lemon under California law, especially if you’ve had defects that were not repaired after several attempts.

