These problems have led many A3 owners to file complaints. If you have one of these models and are experiencing recurring defects, you may be eligible for an Audi lemon law claim.

## Is Your Audi a Lemon?

Know Your Rights Under California Lemon Law

If you drive one of the Audi cars with recurring problems with any of the issues discussed above, you may be dealing with a lemon - beyond just an Audi recall. Under California’s Lemon Law, consumers who purchase or lease new vehicles with significant defects may be entitled to a replacement vehicle, a refund, or other compensation.

In order to qualify for protection under the Audi lemon law in California, your Audi must meet certain conditions, including:

- The vehicle was covered under the original or dealer warranty when the defect was initially reported to Audi; and

- The defect negatively impacts the vehicle’s safety, usability, or value; and

- The defect was not caused by driver neglect or abuse; and

- Audi’s authorized repair technicians have been given a reasonable number of attempts to fix the defect in questions (usually at least two); or

- The vehicle has been out of service for repairs for 30 or more cumulative days.

If you have documentation to prove Audi meets these qualifications, you may be eligible for a claim with an Audi lemon law attorney in California.

